WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.862
Unit 2 reads the report.

2
00:00:01.862 --> 00:00:05.700
It opens on an overview tab,
then a tab for each pillar.

3
00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:07.979
Each test shows its risk and its status,

4
00:00:07.979 --> 00:00:12.750
and selecting a test describes what was
tested and the recommended remediation.

5
00:00:12.750 --> 00:00:16.388
Every test carries three
ratings from Microsoft's rubric,

6
00:00:16.388 --> 00:00:18.662
defined on Learn's terminology page.

7
00:00:18.662 --> 00:00:23.959
Risk level: high means potential
environment-wide exposure until it's mitigated;

8
00:00:23.959 --> 00:00:29.175
medium, moderate exposure; low, defense
in depth or an operational optimization.

9
00:00:29.175 --> 00:00:34.267
User impact: high means many non-privileged
users have to act or be told;

10
00:00:34.267 --> 00:00:36.813
low means only administrators act.

11
00:00:36.813 --> 00:00:41.634
And implementation cost: high is a
program needing ongoing commitment,

12
00:00:41.634 --> 00:00:44.250
medium a project, low a targeted action.

13
00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:48.888
The tool's own source adds two more
risk levels, critical and unranked.

14
00:00:48.888 --> 00:00:52.363
These ratings feed the weighting
you'll meet in Module 3.

15
00:00:52.363 --> 00:00:54.380
They aren't a priority on their own.
